version: 2.0.0
description: |
  `paradigm loop` CLI — authoring side of Gnomon loops (docs/specs/gnomon-loops.md §5,
  build plan LP1). The engine is #loop-files (packages/paradigm-mcp/src/utils/loop-files.ts)
  over #loop-schema (@a-company/gnomon/loops); the Gnomon kernel reads only the compiled JSON.
components:
  loop-cli:
    description: 'paradigm loop new <id> [--example flow-health|green|watch|tidy] [--flow $id] | validate [file|id] [--all] | list (alias ls), each with --json. new writes .paradigm/loops/<id>.yaml from a template (spec Examples A-D on the 8.0 subset) and its compiled <id>.loop.json; validate writes the compiled JSON next to each valid YAML and removes a stale one beside an invalid YAML; list shows validity, autonomy, triggers and whether the compiled JSON is fresh, stale or missing. Issues print as path: CODE: message (8.1 features say "lands in 8.1"). Output via cli-output helpers; library INFO logs quieted unless LOG_LEVEL. Never makes a loop run: Gnomon runs a loop only after a human trusts its content hash. builtin <name> --json [--args <json>] is the thin wrapper Gnomon #loop-check runs inside its loop-check sandbox for the check builtins (paradigm.flow-check, flow-affected, ripple, purpose-validate, drift with autoHeal off, reindex, git.clean): it calls the existing MCP handlers and prints {builtin, ok, passed, failed, error?, result}; exit 0 pass, 1 fail, 2 could not judge.'
    type: command
    anchors:
      - index.ts
    tags: [feature, gnomon, loops, cli]
    tests:
      - index.test.ts
